---
import SiteNav from "../../components/SiteNav.astro";
import BaseHead from "../../components/BaseHead.astro";
import TableOfContents from "../../components/TableOfContents.astro";
import DocSection from "../../components/docs/DocSection.astro";
import DocAlert from "../../components/docs/DocAlert.astro";
import DocNavigation from "../../components/docs/DocNavigation.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
import { wasmSectionPages } from "../../data/wasm-pages";

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: "overview", text: "Overview" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "browser-undo", text: "Browser undo stack" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "model-history", text: "Model-level history" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "wasm-transactions", text: "WASM transactions" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "composition", text: "IME & composition" },
];

const navPages = wasmSectionPages.map((p) => ({
  title: p.titleEn,
  href: `/wasm/${p.slug}`,
  description: p.descEn,
}));
const currentPath = "/wasm/undo-model";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Undo & redo model (Rust + WASM) – contenteditable.lab"
      description="Browser undo vs application history, programmatic DOM changes, and keeping redo coherent when the document state lives in Rust/WASM."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <SiteNav />
    <main class="flex max-w-full m-0 p-0">
      <section
        class="flex-1 flex max-w-[1120px] mx-auto py-7 px-5 pb-10 gap-6 w-full"
      >
        <aside class="hidden lg:block w-[220px] shrink-0">
          <TableOfContents headings={headings} />
        </aside>
        <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
          <header class="mb-8">
            <nav class="mb-4 text-sm">
              <a href="/" class="text-text-muted no-underline">Home</a>
              <span class="text-text-faint mx-2">/</span>
              <a href="/wasm" class="text-text-muted no-underline">Wasm</a>
              <span class="text-text-faint mx-2">/</span>
              <span class="text-text-primary">Undo & redo model</span>
            </nav>
            <h1 class="text-3xl leading-tight m-0 mb-2">Undo & redo model</h1>
            <p class="m-0 text-[0.95rem] text-text-secondary">
              Ctrl+Z can mean “browser undo” or “editor command”—mixing them with a
              Rust model requires an explicit policy.
            </p>
          </header>

          <article
            class="rounded-xl border border-border-light bg-bg-surface p-6 px-7 text-[0.9rem] leading-[1.7]"
          >
            <DocSection id="overview" title="Overview">
              <p class="m-0 mb-4">
                See also{" "}
                <a href="/editor/history-management" class="text-accent-primary underline"
                  >Editor → History management</a
                > for product-neutral patterns. Here we stress <strong>who owns
                undo</strong> when part of the stack is WASM and part is{" "}
                <code>contenteditable</code>.
              </p>
            </DocSection>

            <DocSection id="browser-undo" title="Browser undo stack">
              <p class="m-0 mb-4">
                The browser maintains its own undo history for editable regions.
                Programmatic DOM updates, <code>execCommand</code>, and some
                frameworks can <strong>clear</strong> or <strong>split</strong> that
                stack—behavior varies by browser.
              </p>
            </DocSection>

            <DocSection id="model-history" title="Model-level history">
              <p class="m-0 mb-4">
                Robust editors usually implement <strong>inverse operations</strong> or
                snapshots on the <strong>document model</strong> in Rust, then
                re-render the DOM. Browser undo may be disabled or synchronized via{" "}
                <code>beforeinput</code> interception where supported.
              </p>
              <DocAlert type="warning">
                <p class="m-0 text-sm">
                  Two independent undo stacks (browser + app) confuse users—pick
                  one authoritative history for text edits.
                </p>
              </DocAlert>
            </DocSection>

            <DocSection id="wasm-transactions" title="WASM transactions">
              <p class="m-0 mb-4">
                Batch model changes into transactions in Rust; expose “undo” as
                applying inverse ops or rolling back to a checkpoint. Crossing into
                JS only for DOM patches reduces mismatches.
              </p>
            </DocSection>

            <DocSection id="composition" title="IME & composition">
              <p class="m-0 mb-4">
                Undo during IME composition is especially fragile. Often you
                defer history commits until composition ends—aligns with{" "}
                <a href="/wasm/ime-and-composition" class="text-accent-primary underline"
                  >IME & composition</a
                >.
              </p>
            </DocSection>

            <DocNavigation
              current={currentPath}
              pages={navPages}
              title="Wasm guides"
            />
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
